infographic sequence-pyramid-simple
data
  title Log levels are a contract: who has to act?
  desc Severity climbs toward the apex while volume falls — keep Error rare or the pager goes numb
  sequences
    - label Error — a human must act
      desc Feeds alerts and pages the on-call. Log expected client failures here and the pager habituates until real errors drown.
    - label Warn — degraded but self-healed
      desc A retry succeeded, a fallback engaged. Nobody wakes; the aggregate rate is the early warning reviewed tomorrow.
    - label Info — sparse state changes
      desc Deploys, connections established, jobs completed — worth grepping later. If it fires on every request, it is volume, not signal.
    - label Debug — off in production
      desc Switched on per-incident; assume nobody sees it. Highest volume, lowest stakes.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #0ea5e9 #14b8a6
